config BR2_PACKAGE_VINX_LVGL
	bool "vinx-lvgl"
	depends on BR2_i386
	help
	  LVGL v9 as a shared library for the machine's own C compilers:
	  `tcc gui.c -llvgl` paints widgets on /dev/fb0 (the Bochs DRM
	  framebuffer the screen panel shows) and reads the pointer and
	  keyboard from evdev. Headers land in /usr/include/lvgl with the
	  config at /usr/include/lv_conf.h, the layout both gcc and tcc
	  resolve. Mainline Buildroot has no lvgl package; the vinx-
	  prefix marks it as this tree's own. ~+1.3 MB compressed.

	  Chinese text works out of the box: the rootfs overlay ships a
	  GB2312 bitmap font at /usr/share/fonts/cjk16.bin and
	  lv_binfont_create loads it at runtime -- see lvdemo(1) and the
	  linux-vm skill.

	  https://lvgl.io
